I roughed out a quick hack to create a new command which would allow
the user to show vanquished monsters in mid-game for 3.4.0 (using the
same function you can use when you die/ascend).  It was expanded upon
and patchified by Dylan O'Donnell and placed as a new extended command
#vanquished.

I just updated it for 3.4.3 and dumped it on my server
(http://planetexpress.homedns.org/nethack/listvanq.patch).  At any
time, you can use #vanquished to see a complete list of monsters that
have been killed (by you, a pet, or a trap).

This is the first time I've used diff to create a patch, so let me
know if it doesn't work properly.

To answer your question, the create monster spell/scroll/wand will
only create non-extinct monsters, and never create monsters that have
the NOGEN flag.  The monster spell summon nasties ignores extinction
and the NOGEN flag, meaning you can kill more than 120 minotaurs in a
game (just one example).

